-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/hoa/documents/#article","headline":"What to Look for in HOA Documents Before Buying","description":"The HOA documents to obtain before you buy on the Grand Strand, what each one reveals, and the red flags we look for when we read them for a client.","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/hoa/documents/","author":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/about/#devin-day"},"reviewedBy":{"@type":"Person","name":"Timothy Nash","alternateName":"Tim Nash","jobTitle":"Broker-in-Charge"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"datePublished":"2026-07-27","dateModified":"2026-10-28","inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://chapter3realty.com/og-image.jpg","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/hoa/documents/#webpage"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"What to Look for in HOA Documents Before Buying"},"keywords":"what to look for in HOA documents, HOA document review, HOA governing documents South Carolina"}</script>
-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/hoa/documents/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What HOA documents should I get before buying?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The declaration or master deed, the bylaws, and the current rules and regulations. This year's budget, the balance sheet and income statement, and the most recent reserve study. Board meeting minutes for the last twelve to twenty-four months. The master insurance certificate and any litigation disclosure. An estoppel or resale statement showing what is owed on the unit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When do I get the HOA documents?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually during your due diligence period, and often later than is useful. In South Carolina's 2026 HOA report only 32 percent of complainants said they received the governing documents before purchase, while 53 percent received them after. Ask for them as early as possible and treat slow delivery as information."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which document has the rules I have to follow?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually three. The declaration or master deed creates the obligations that run with the property, the bylaws govern how the association operates, and the rules and regulations are the day-to-day list that the board can change most easily."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the biggest red flags in HOA documents?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Thin reserves against aging components, several years of flat dues while costs rose, active litigation, a high share of unpaid assessments, a large single owner, and restrictions that conflict with how you plan to use the property."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the seller have to tell me there is an HOA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. South Carolina's residential property condition disclosure requires a seller to disclose that the property is governed by a homeowners association. That disclosure does not tell you what the rules say. That is why the documents matter."}}]}</script>
